  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1223197,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1943 - The Battle of Midway (Commodore Amiga)\n\nRelive the pivotal Battle of Midway in this thrilling vertical scrolling shooter, a direct sequel to the classic 1942! Take to the skies as a lone P-38 Lightning pilot, tasked with single-handedly turning the tide of WWII against the formidable Japanese navy. The game plunges you into intense aerial and naval combat off the coast of Midway Atoll, culminating in a showdown with the mighty battleship Yamato.\n\nGameplay retains the familiar feel of its predecessor, with a single life and a rechargeable energy meter adding a layer of strategic challenge. Utilize standard attacks and special actions – including a loop maneuver and powerful, health-draining special attacks – to overcome waves of enemy aircraft and colossal boss battles. Destroying enemy formations rewards you with valuable power-ups, from automatic guns and artillery shells to a futuristic laser! Keep an eye out for hidden animal icons and the iconic Yashichi symbol to restore health and gain wingmen. Prepare for a relentless assault and a historically inspired, yet dramatically embellished, aerial war!"
    },
